{"kind":"artifact","text":"The citation guard at its real boundary, internal/app on exact head 9cd8e8f0aa4f877b8213283d1f35cc687e500a77. BuildActRequest refuses a supersession whose target the documentation still cites, so every surface that reaches the log passes the check. It previously lived only in cmd/gs, and the MCP surface submits a supersession directly, so a retirement filed there skipped it — which is how main went red today.\n\nAct.CitedOK carries the migration escape. Only a surface that can put the choice to a person sets it: gs supersede and gs batch pass --cited-ok through, and the MCP tool has no way to ask for it. gs batch keeps its whole-file pre-flight, now calling the same exported guard, so a batch that cannot land cleanly still lands nothing; and batch targets written as dollar-labels, which the pre-flight cannot resolve, now reach the boundary check for the first time.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by reading: removing the boundary check fails the new internal/app test and both cmd/gs tests, because there is one implementation where there were three.\n\nIt rests on 7f4416ae, the assert that recorded the hole.","body":{"commit":"9cd8e8f0aa4f877b8213283d1f35cc687e500a77","path":"internal/app"}}